@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.dev/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.dev/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.dev/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# Retrospective summary for PR #329 (closes issue #326), written for issue
# #352's representative sample. Picked as the "new-feature/schema-design"
# variety slot: this is the PR that introduced the agp: vocabulary and
# shapes this very file format depends on -- a pleasingly self-referential
# choice for a sample meant to stress-test that schema. Two genuine
# decision-point forks are documented in the PR body itself (both verified
# empirically against the real reasoner, not just reasoned about on paper),
# so this file uses two agp:Decision entries, unlike most of the other
# sample files which have zero.
#
# ghpull:329 asserted as bl:PullRequest/bl:WorkItem; ghissues:326 referenced
# only as an object (bl:closesIssue, prov:used), not typed bl:Issue.
#
# Both agp:Decision entries are given named session:-scoped IRIs (matching
# pr-300.ttl's and pr-348.ttl's convention) rather than blank nodes, so a
# review dashboard query (provenance/queries/all_decision_points.sparql,
# whose own header calls it exactly that) can cite and reload the same
# identifier across runs -- a blank node label is unstable across parses
# and gives a reviewer nothing linkable.
#
# Timestamps from `gh pr view 329 --json commits,mergedAt`: four commits
# spanning 2026-07-31T21:18:39Z through 21:35:41Z (a 17-minute window),
# mergedAt 2026-07-31T22:02:13Z the same evening -- one continuous session,
# startedAtTime is the first commit's authoredDate.

ghpull:329 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "backlog: agentprov vocabulary for agent-session/transcript-summary provenance (#326)" ;
    bl:number 329 ;
    bl:state bl:Closed ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:326 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr329 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:326 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-07-31T21:18:39Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-07-31T22:02:13Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr329Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "First concrete slice of the agent-provenance epic #306: added backlog/ontology/agentprov-vocabulary.ttl defining the agp: namespace (agp:AgentSession, agp:TranscriptSummary, agp:Decision classes; agp:summaryText, agp:reasoningFor, agp:transcriptRef, agp:decisionPoint, agp:alternative, agp:parentSession properties), reusing PROV-O terms directly (prov:Entity, prov:Activity, prov:SoftwareAgent) rather than redeclaring them, matching the pattern bl: already used for doap:Project. Added matching SHACL shapes (agentprov-shapes.ttl) and tests/agentprov_ontology.rs validating both against this repo's own shacl crate, using a fictional PR #999 toy fixture rather than real transcript data. Deliberately scoped OUT of this PR: the real grounding example, the SPARQL query library, and the CLAUDE.md workflow step -- all of which need this vocabulary to exist first, and are exactly what later PRs (#331, #334, and this backfill itself) built on top of it." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:329 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr329NoDomainDecision, session:pr329DisjointnessDecision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr329 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr329NoDomainDecision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "agp:summaryText was given no rdfs:domain, even though it's the only property shared by both agp:TranscriptSummary and agp:Decision. A single-class domain (e.g. agp:TranscriptSummary) would, under RDFS entailment, wrongly classify every agp:Decision as also being an agp:TranscriptSummary purely because it uses the same property. Verified empirically, both directions: reinstating the domain on a scratch copy and rerunning the reasoner over the toy fixture produced a plain agp:Decision individual as a false positive result for a SELECT ?x WHERE { ?x a agp:TranscriptSummary } query; removing it (as shipped) did not." ;
    agp:alternative "Declaring rdfs:domain agp:TranscriptSummary on agp:summaryText, rejected because it entails every agp:Decision is also an agp:TranscriptSummary under RDFS semantics, confirmed as a real false-positive query result rather than a theoretical concern." .

session:pr329DisjointnessDecision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Added agp:Decision owl:disjointWith agp:AgentSession, agp:TranscriptSummary explicitly, since Decision has no PROV-O superclass to inherit disjointness through the way AgentSession/TranscriptSummary do (via prov:Activity/prov:Entity, which this repo's own prov-o.ttl test fixture already declares disjoint). Given a known reasoner panic bug on file for under-tested ontology axioms in this same file family (#298), the full multi-type grounding fixture (sessions, summaries, decisions, PR stub, agents together) was run through apply_ontologies with the new disjointness axiom active to rule out a similar crash -- completed cleanly." ;
    agp:alternative "Leaving Decision without an explicit disjointness axiom, rejected because it would silently omit inconsistency detection between Decision and the two PROV-O-derived classes that a symmetric design otherwise provides for free." .
